          "ruleId": "built-in:code",
          "aspect": "correctness",
          "severity": "high",
          "state": "open",
          "title": "Missing review metadata does not fail the scan",
          "description": "The exit status tests only StaleCount. If files are reported as missing but none are stale, the command prints the missing entries and nevertheless exits successfully. This can allow unreviewed files to pass a CI quality gate.",
          "recommendation": "Return exit code 1 when either stale or missing files exist, or explicitly document and expose an option if missing metadata is intentionally non-blocking.",
