          "aspect": "correctness",
          "severity": "medium",
          "state": "open",
          "title": "Invalid numeric option values are reinterpreted as positional arguments",
          "description": "Both parsers increment index inside int.TryParse. When parsing fails, execution continues through the same if/else chain with args[index] now referring to the invalid value. That value can consequently become the review file or report repository path instead of producing the intended invalid-option error.",
          "recommendation": "Inspect args[index \u002B 1] without changing index, throw a targeted ArgumentException when parsing fails, and increment index only after successful validation. Consider extracting a shared numeric-option parser.",
